## CI/CD

Default GitHub Actions workflow runs **quality + security** checks only (no repo secrets required).

After adding these secrets in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions:

| Secret | Used for |
|--------|----------|
| `SONAR_TOKEN` | SonarQube analysis |
| `SONAR_HOST_URL` | SonarQube server URL |
| `AWS_ROLE_ARN` | SST deploy to AWS |

Copy the extended pipeline:

```sh
cp .github/workflows/ci-extended.yml.example .github/workflows/ci-extended.yml
git add .github/workflows/ci-extended.yml
git commit -m "ci: enable SonarQube and deploy pipeline"
git push
```

Reusable workflows are loaded from `{{idpRepo}}` at ref `{{idpRef}}`.

## Dependency updates (Dependabot)

This repo includes `.github/dependabot.yml` for weekly npm and GitHub Actions update PRs.

Enable security alerts in GitHub → **Settings** → **Code security** → turn on **Dependabot alerts** and **Dependabot security updates**.

